.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "build_fuzzygene" "build_fuzzygene"
.SH NAME
build_fuzzygene \- Build an untrained neuro-fuzzy gene regulatory network model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIbuild_fuzzygene(\fBx\fR as <generic> GeneExpressionData, 
\fBprior\fR as <generic> PriorNetwork = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBconfig\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneConfig = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Build an untrained neuro-fuzzy gene regulatory network model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBx\fB \fR\- the gene expression matrix (rows = genes, columns = samples). 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior\fB \fR\- 
 an optional prior regulatory network created by the \fBbnlearn\fR package (\fBprior_edges\fR);
 when omitted the candidate regulators are selected by correlation only.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBconfig\fB \fR\- 
 the configuration created by \fBfuzzygene::fuzzygene_config\fR; \fBNothing\fR uses the defaults.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment (unused). 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an untrained model object
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The expression matrix provides the training data: when it carries \fBTimePoints\fR with at
 least three distinct values the model learns the lagged map `x(t+1) = F(x(t))`,
 otherwise it learns the static map `x_g = F(regulators)`. The prior network supplies
 TF-to-target edges that are used to order (not to force) the candidate inputs.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
